<section class="ref-group"><h2>Battles <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tellaru"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Tellaru</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 9th century</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Tellaru was fought in the mid-ninth century at Tellaru, near Vandavasi in northern Tamil Nadu, where the Pallava king Nandivarman III defeated the Pandyas…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-teutoburg-forest"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-the-teutoburg-forest.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Teutoburg Forest</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 9 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Teutoburg Forest was fought in 9 CE in Germania, where Germanic tribes led by Arminius ambushed and destroyed three Roman legions under Publius…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-idistaviso"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-idistaviso.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Idistaviso</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 16 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Idistaviso was fought in 16 CE on a plain near the Weser in northern Germany, between eight Roman legions with auxiliaries under Germanicus and a…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-angrivarian-wall"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-the-angrivarian-wall.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Angrivarian Wall</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 16 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Angrivarian Wall was fought in 16 CE between Roman legions under Germanicus and Germanic tribes led by Arminius of the Cherusci.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-baduhenna-wood"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-baduhenna-wood.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Baduhenna Wood</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 28 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Baduhenna Wood was fought in 28 CE in Frisia, in the present-day Netherlands, between the rebellious Frisii and Roman troops.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rhandeia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-rhandeia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Rhandeia</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 62</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Rhandeia was fought in 62 CE in Armenia during the war between Rome and Parthia over the Armenian throne.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-beth-horon-66"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-beth-horon-66.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Beth Horon (66)</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 66 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Beth Horon was fought in the autumn of 66 CE, when Jewish rebels ambushed the retreating army of Cestius Gallus, the Roman governor of Syria, in the Beth…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mons-graupius"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-mons-graupius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Mons Graupius</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 83 or 84</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Mons Graupius was fought in 83 or 84 CE in north-eastern Scotland between a Roman army under Gnaeus Julius Agricola and the Caledonians, whose leader…</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Wars &amp; campaigns <span class="n">10</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-invasion-of-kush"><span class="enc-name">Aksumite invasion of Kush</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · c. 4th century CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Aksumite invasion of Kush refers to military expeditions by the Aksumite Empire into the Kingdom of Kush in the c. 4th century CE, most notably under King Ezana.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/early-muslim-conquests"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/early-muslim-conquests.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Early Muslim conquests</span><span class="enc-type">War · 7th century</span><span class="enc-snip">The early Muslim conquests were the rapid expansion of the Arab Muslim state in the 7th century, following the death of the Prophet Muhammad.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/northern-crusades"><span class="enc-name">Northern Crusades</span><span class="enc-type">War · 12th–15th century</span><span class="enc-snip">The Northern Crusades were the crusades waged by Catholic Danish, Swedish and German rulers and military orders against the pagan peoples around the Baltic Sea from the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/swedish-novgorodian-wars"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/swedish-novgorodian-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Swedish–Novgorodian Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War · 12th–14th century</span><span class="enc-snip">The Swedish–Novgorodian Wars were a series of conflicts between Sweden and the Novgorod Republic over Finland, Karelia and the trade routes of the Gulf of Finland and…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mongol-invasions-of-anatolia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mongol-invasions-of-anatolia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mongol invasions of Anatolia</span><span class="enc-type">War · 13th century</span><span class="enc-snip">The Mongol invasions of Anatolia were the campaigns by which the Mongol Empire subdued the Seljuk Sultanate of Rum in the mid-13th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/croatian-ottoman-wars"><span class="enc-name">Croatian–Ottoman wars</span><span class="enc-type">War · 15th–16th century</span><span class="enc-snip">The Croatian–Ottoman wars were a long series of conflicts between the Kingdom of Croatia and the Ottoman Empire from the fifteenth century to the end of the sixteenth.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/russo-crimean-wars"><span class="enc-name">Russo-Crimean Wars</span><span class="enc-type">War · 16th century</span><span class="enc-snip">The Russo-Crimean Wars were a series of conflicts in the sixteenth century between the Grand Duchy of Moscow, later the Tsardom of Russia, and the Crimean Khanate…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/roman-conquest-of-britain"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/roman-conquest-of-britain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Roman conquest of Britain</span><span class="enc-type">War · 43–84 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Roman conquest of Britain began with the invasion ordered by Emperor Claudius in 43 CE and continued in stages over the next four decades.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/roman-parthian-war-of-58-63"><span class="enc-name">Roman–Parthian War of 58–63</span><span class="enc-type">War · 58–63</span><span class="enc-snip">The Roman–Parthian War of 58–63 was fought between the Roman Empire and Parthia over control of Armenia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/first-jewish-roman-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/first-jewish-roman-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">First Jewish–Roman War</span><span class="enc-type">War · Revolt · 66–73</span><span class="enc-snip">The First Jewish–Roman War was the revolt of the Jews of Judaea against Roman rule from 66 to 73 CE.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Revolts &amp; revolutions <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/great-illyrian-revolt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/great-illyrian-revolt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Great Illyrian Revolt</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 6–9 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Great Illyrian Revolt was a rising of the peoples of Pannonia and Dalmatia against Roman rule from 6 to 9 CE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aisso"><span class="enc-name">Aissó</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 9th century</span><span class="enc-snip">Aissó, or Aizo, was a Gothic noble of the Spanish March who rebelled against Frankish rule in 826.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/varendra-rebellion"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/varendra-rebellion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Varendra rebellion</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · late 11th century</span><span class="enc-snip">The Varendra rebellion was a revolt of the Kaivartas, a community of boatmen and cultivators, against the Pala dynasty in northern Bengal in the late eleventh century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/lulin"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lulin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Lülin</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 17–25</span><span class="enc-snip">The Lülin, or 'Green Forest', were a rebel movement that arose around 17 CE in the hills of Hubei against Wang Mang's Xin dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/red-eyebrows"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/red-eyebrows.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Red Eyebrows</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 18–27</span><span class="enc-snip">The Red Eyebrows were a peasant rebel movement that rose in Shandong around 18 CE against Wang Mang's Xin dynasty, its fighters painting their eyebrows red to tell…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/boudican-revolt"><span class="enc-name">Boudican revolt</span><span class="enc-type">Revolt · 60–61</span><span class="enc-snip">The Boudican revolt was an uprising of the Iceni and neighbouring peoples of Britain against Roman rule in 60 or 61 CE, led by Boudica, widow of the Iceni king…</span></a></li></ul></section>
